 ## Background
-FIDE was introduced by Andrei-Timotei Ardelean, Michael Fischer, Tim Weyrich, and Tomáš Iser in 2026 [S1, unofficial]. It builds on the principles of CMA-ES [Hansen 2006] and diffusion models [Li and He 2025], addressing the limitations of black-box optimization methods that rely on scalar loss values [S1, unofficial]. The method was validated across diverse inverse problems including camera pose estimation, robot arm estimation, path tracing, vector splines, and Voronoi shaders [S1, unofficial].
